       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The current FDA-approved amlodipine label lists a maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults, so 50 mg is not within the labeled maximum. I can't verify the claim, and it conflicts with the labeling as I know it.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a labeled dose.** Give me 2.5, 5, or 10 mg once daily and I'll enter it now.\n- **Check the label yourself.** If you have a source showing a higher maximum, please review it with pharmacy.\n- **Use another route.** If you believe this dose is clinically necessary, your pharmacist or attending can verify and enter it through the hospital's dose-override process.\n\nIf you're trying to get stronger blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, I can enter a combination, such as amlodipine 10 mg plus an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. You would need to specify the drug and dose."
